{"chunk_id": "d3205ac650cf", "text": "Krishna, Bhima, and Arjuna arrive in disguise at the court of King Jarasandha. Jarasandha immediately suspects them, noting that true Brahmanas observing the Snataka vow would not be adorned with garlands and bearing the marks of bowstrings. Krishna replies with clever ambiguity, justifying their appearance and behavior while hinting at their warrior nature and their intention to confront an enemy. Jarasandha insists he has done them no wrong and defends his conduct as a righteous Kshatriya. Krishna then openly accuses him of imprisoning many kings in order to sacrifice them to Rudra. Declaring this act sinful and tyrannical, Krishna reveals their identities\u2014himself and the sons of Pandu\u2014and challenges Jarasandha: either release the captive monarchs or face death in battle. The passage frames the confrontation as a moral and dharmic reckoning.\nKrishna reveals himself and the Pandavas to Jarasandha, condemns his capture of kings for sacrifice, and challenges him to release them or fight.\nThemes: challenge before battle, dharma and kingship, human sacrifice condemned, revealed identities, warrior honor", "vector": [0.012018927372992039, -0.026570992544293404, -0.00484395120292902, 0.004624996334314346, -0.009101777337491512, 0.023889638483524323, -0.01440384890884161, -0.005409864708781242, -0.018890734761953354, -0.009809168986976147, 0.013514555990695953, 0.0036615957506000996, 0.0023562891874462366, 0.009593583643436432, -0.003890656167641282, -0.010509824380278587, 0.043979573994874954, -0.013474133796989918, 0.031691163778305054, -0.013110332190990448, -0.006295789033174515, -0.009910225868225098, -0.01143953949213028, 0.01612853817641735, -0.026638362556695938, 0.019025476649403572, 0.004139927681535482, -0.015387460589408875, 4.894900121144019e-05, -0.017435528337955475, -0.01677529700100422, -0.01374361664056778, -0.0007819208549335599, -0.001822376623749733, -0.023620156571269035, 0.007478144485503435, -0.0088